  "notes": "Curated real-world C source from musl libc: all of src/string (74 .c), all of src/stdio (116 .c), all of src/stdlib (22 .c), all of src/ctype (37 .c), double-precision math core (73 .c) plus float/long-double variants of sqrt, fabs, floor, ceil and Bessel j0/j1/jn, plus src/prng/rand.c and src/malloc/mallocng/malloc.c (named in the brief; neither lives in src/stdlib -- musl's malloc is in src/malloc/mallocng/). Excluded: math *_data tables, __rem_pio2_large.c, other float/long-double math variants, Bessel float variants, stdio getc.h/putc.h and ctype table headers (alpha.h, casemap.h, nonspacing.h, punct.h, wide.h), and arch-specific subdirectories. Per the repo COPYRIGHT, math code is largely derived from Sun/FreBSD sources under permissive terms and labelled in the individual files. Fetch was paced (one request at a time with a delay) after parallel requests hit a transient GitHub MCP rate limit; all 335 files fetched, 0 failed."
